enviPat / pyEnvipat -- Authors
==============================

Original algorithm authors (R package `enviPat`, EAWAG)
---------------------------------------------------------

- Martin Loos <martin.loos@eawag.ch>
- Christian Gerber

Reference:
  Loos, M., Gerber, C., Corona, F., Hollender, J., Singer, H. (2015)
  "Accelerated Isotope Fine Structure Calculation Using Pruned
  Transition Trees", Analytical Chemistry.
  doi:10.1021/acs.analchem.5b00941

Python port maintainer
-----------------------

- Johannes Boog <johannesboog@yahoo.de>

  Maintains the Python port (`pyEnvipat`) of the original R package.
  The port is a derivative work: its C extension vendors the original
  algorithm C sources unmodified or with structural (non-algorithmic)
  extraction, and its Python layer reproduces the R package's
  documented behavior, with any deviations disclosed in the relevant
  merge request. The porter is credited here as maintainer of the
  Python port, not as author of the underlying algorithms.

Other historical contributors (R package, pre-port)
-----------------------------------------------------

- Artem Tarasov
- wkumler

See the git history of the upstream R package
(https://github.com/blosloos/enviPat) for the full contribution record.
